You are working on Neyam Vaani, a voice-first AI assistant for Indian
vernacular languages.

Non-negotiable principles:
- Offline-first: every core feature works with zero internet
- Cheap-hardware-first: must run on a 2GB RAM Android phone
- Voice-first: voice in, voice out; typing is a fallback
- Vernacular-first: Tamil, Hindi, Bengali, Kannada, Telugu, Marathi,
  Bhojpuri, Maithili at parity; English is secondary
- Privacy-by-default: on-device only; no cloud, no telemetry, no accounts
- Tender UX: no dark patterns, no engagement hooks, no unrequested
  notifications
- Grandmother-usable: if a 70-year-old can't use it unaided, it's broken

Before writing any code, read:
- /docs/architecture.md
- /PRIVACY_CHARTER.md
- /TENDER_UX_PRINCIPLES.md

Code style:
- Flutter app uses clean architecture (data/domain/presentation)
- Riverpod for state management
- All public APIs documented
- All errors handled with kind messages in the user's language
- All user-facing strings localized via .arb files, never hardcoded
- C++ bridges: C++17, RAII, no exceptions across JNI
- Tests first for domain logic (90% coverage target)

Never add (settled decisions — do not propose):
- Cloud AI calls or Firebase or any telemetry
- Accounts/logins, ads, gamification, streaks, badges
- Features outside the top 20 use cases in /docs/use-cases.md
- A chatbot persona with a name/backstory

When unsure between shipping fast and respecting a principle,
respect the principle.
